{%- comment -%}
  Author box for long-form guides.

  Renders only when the article's author field names the site's author, so an
  article genuinely written by someone else does not get attributed to him.
  The claims here are the ones the About page supports; nothing is added that
  is not already stated and verifiable there.

  Usage: {% render 'sbs-author', author: article.author %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign known_author = 'James Joyner IV' -%}

{%- if author == known_author -%}
  <aside class="sbs-author" aria-labelledby="sbs-author-h">
    <p class="sbs-author__eyebrow">Written by</p>
    <h2 class="sbs-author__name" id="sbs-author-h">
      <a href="/pages/about" rel="author">{{ known_author }}</a>
    </h2>
    <p class="sbs-author__role">Senior Software Engineer &middot; 25 years in technology</p>
    <p class="sbs-author__bio">
      Platform and infrastructure engineering &mdash; Linux, Kubernetes, OpenStack, Ansible,
      Terraform, Docker, GitLab CI, Prometheus and Grafana &mdash; now applied to directing
      Claude Code through real production work. Site Builder Stack was built with the method
      it documents, including the parts that went wrong.
    </p>
    <p class="sbs-author__more">
      <a href="/pages/about">More about James</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/pages/contact">Get in touch</a>
    </p>
  </aside>
{%- endif -%}
